cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this method, please cite it as below. The French corpus is authoritative."
title: "WORKING REFERENCE: the reference that works — the corpus as a function"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Noto"
    given-names: "Julien-Pierre"
    alias: "JP Noto"
version: "0.1.7"
date-released: "2026-08-11"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/JP-Noto/WORKING-REFERENCE"
abstract: >-
  WORKING REFERENCE claims that a reference corpus is a function, not a document:
  a constant (the invariant earned through explicit gates) plus variables,
  instantiated by the reference layer from the declared state of the work in
  progress, served (never bulk-loaded) and sealed (every serving decision is
  traceable). Medium is a variable: one more medium costs a generator and a
  bench, never a second reference layer. Current proof rank, stated honestly:
  hypothesis (author's verdict, 2026-08-11) — the mechanisms exist separately in real
  use by a single practitioner; their unification under one function is untested.
